{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed","id":1539842,"title":"How do signature characters designed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-05T04:38:24-07:00","id":1539842,"title":"How do signature characters designed?","content":"We all know every splat have a signature character for each faction. So how do authors design them? I\u2019m sure they must have much discussion before released one<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T10:10:57-07:00","id":1539862,"title":"","content":"That's a fun question,i don't know either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:46:40-07:00","id":1539874,"title":"","content":"A lot of them were PCs or NPCs the authors created for internal play test games, but were kept around through editions. Keep in mind that the concept of &quot;signature&quot; characters was somewhat organic rather than intentional. It was sample characters to illustrate aspects of a splat, that became signature character over time.<br /> <br /> More time seems to go into them these days simply it went from an emergent thing, to a purposeful thing. &quot;This was our favorite Nosferatu character from our playtest, so lets have him be the sample character in the book,&quot; is a lot easier than trying to craft a character without any real context beyond, &quot;make something emblematic of the splat, but not two-dimensional, and try to show off the variety of character types in the game so avoid making them too similar in cultural backgrounds.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:47:24-07:00","id":1539887,"title":"","content":"I would say that they began as test characters for a game that the authors used and liked enough to include in future books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T16:04:20-07:00","id":1539893,"title":"","content":"I have a rough idea on which ones belong to some writers, know which ones do belong to who, but always wandered who play tested Lucita. I bet on Cynthia Summers.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T17:02:29-07:00","id":1539897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed#post1539842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all know every splat have a signature character for each faction. So how do authors design them? I\u2019m sure they must have much discussion before released one</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt there was much discussion at all. It was just a cool thing to do.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the biggest character derrailment was when they tried to make Lucita more like a traditional Lasombra and everyone hated it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T17:18:57-07:00","id":1539898,"title":"","content":"What they did with Lucita wasn't well received by VTM fans and I'm curious what the mindset was that she needed &quot;fixing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T17:33:06-07:00","id":1539899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1539898#post1539898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What they did with Lucita wasn't well received by VTM fans and I'm curious what the mindset was that she needed &quot;fixing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is hilarious that they made her Sabbat so she could be more representative of a typical Lasombra and then they had the Lasombra join the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that Lasombra Antitribu were hugely popular in LARP to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:25:16-07:00","id":1539904,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, they sort of came about as a marketing tool on the WWGS website around the time the fiction publishing arm started to really be a thing (when they were putting out material by Michael Moorcock, Harlan Elison, and others in addition to the first WoD novels). The Werewolf ones, for example, started as the characters from the comic book Bill Bridges's brother did (that originally ran in White Wolf Magazine before being collected in the 2nd ed core book), while the Changeling ones were from Jackie Cassada's Immortal Eyes trilogy. But it wasn't until the revised editions that it was decided for each Clan/Tribe/etc. to have one. Sometimes these would be picked from a previously published character (the Silent Strider one appeared in the original tribebook's opening comic IIRC), while others were just invented whole cloth from scratch (the Glasswalker, for example). The most unique one was the Fianna, which was the character creation example Diedre Brooks did for Werewolf revised. Apparently, Ethan Skemp just liked it so much, he made it the tribe's signature character. <br /> I think the Lasombra, Malkavian, Tzimisce, and Assamite ones started as Dark Ages signature characters and just sort of got ported into revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T10:55:02-07:00","id":1539933,"title":"","content":"Unpopular opinion but I never liked the Signature Characters from Revised Edition<br /> <br /> To get back on topic, I know for a fact that some of the VTM signature characters were originally playtest characters for Dark Ages that got backported into Revised and the Clan Novel series, so I get why they were included but they never really did anything for me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-06-2024, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T13:30:53-07:00","id":1539940,"title":"","content":"do we know if the First Cabal are signature characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T14:22:37-07:00","id":1539946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1539940#post1539940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do we know if the First Cabal are signature characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they were the signature characters (such as they were) for Mage the Sorcerers Crusade, and are depicted in the art work of each Tradition's write up in that book. <br /> <br /> I am unable to recall if the Order of Reason characters were ever officially named.<br /> <br /> <br /> I still kind of lament that a WoD &quot;Pulp Age&quot; was never a real thing, because I think you could have a lot of fun with that. Mage and Werewolf pretty much already have characters for it, and Changeling is pretty easy. But also it just amuses me to think of things like making the Ventrue and Toreador ones be a married couple based on Nick and Nora Charles from The Thin Man (complete with a little ghoul terrier).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T14:55:21-07:00","id":1539949,"title":"","content":"Signature characters under the right author can be quite successful. Look at what Margaret Weis did with pregenerated characters like Raistlin Majere or R.A. Salvatore with Drizzt. Hesha was my favorite signature character from the Followers of Set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T16:21:53-07:00","id":1539957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1539949#post1539949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signature characters under the right author can be quite successful. Look at what Margaret Weis did with pregenerated characters like Raistlin Majere or R.A. Salvatore with Drizzt. Hesha was my favorite signature character from the Followers of Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raistlin and Driz'zt are not signature characters, though, and I'm not sure they're pregens, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T16:49:16-07:00","id":1539958,"title":"","content":"I recall when Margret Weis did Soul Forge &amp; Brothers in Arms and she mentioned in the introduction that she saw a brief description of the characters of the Dragonlance books and she was attracted to the mage and wanted to figure out why he had hourglass shape eyes and gold colored skin.<br /> <br /> She was intrigued by him and created a background for him and to me he sounded like a pregenerated character of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T03:51:39-07:00","id":1539983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1539957#post1539957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raistlin and Driz'zt are not signature characters, though, and I'm not sure they're pregens, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raistlin first appeared as a pregen in <i>DL1 / Dragons of Despair</i> in 1984. The &quot;hourglass eyes&quot; get a mention, but the description of him in that book wasn't much more than &quot;He's a magic user&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T05:59:01-07:00","id":1539985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1539983#post1539983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raistlin first appeared as a pregen in <i>DL1 / Dragons of Despair</i> in 1984. The &quot;hourglass eyes&quot; get a mention, but the description of him in that book wasn't much more than &quot;He's a magic user&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drizzt was created in an elevator when RA Salvatore was asked to come up with a pitch for a novel on the spot and he came up with dark elf and panther as part of his &quot;barbarian novel&quot; to give him a cool mentor.<br /> <br /> Then he became the star.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T10:58:21-07:00","id":1539997,"title":"","content":"Good to know that Raistlin was a pregen. Driz'zt, though, is an OC for the novel.<br /> <br /> Either way, neither of them is a Signature Character, even if Driz'zt became a whole trope in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T14:30:36-07:00","id":1540014,"title":"","content":"So... while I get the desire to debate this...<br /> <br /> There's no such thing as a &quot;signature character&quot; outside of WW games. It's not a defined concept anywhere else. It's a WoD-ism that WW used to describe characters that were regularly used in splat pages/sample fiction/etc. There's no industry standard to point to, no broad concept here. Other games do the same thing, but nobody called them signature characters except as reference to WW's' approach to it. D&amp;D has never tagged specific characters as &quot;signature characters&quot; to claim some are and some aren't.<br /> <br /> Outside of WW specific games... it's not a phrase with any distinct meaning. There's no functional way to have a debate over whether X character is or isn't a signature character in Call of Cthulhu the same way you can argue that the Voerman sisters aren't signature characters for VtM despite being iconic Malkavians thanks to the Bloodlines 1 marketing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T15:28:30-07:00","id":1540018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1540014#post1540014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... while I get the desire to debate this...<br /> <br /> There's no such thing as a &quot;signature character&quot; outside of WW games. It's not a defined concept anywhere else. It's a WoD-ism that WW used to describe characters that were regularly used in splat pages/sample fiction/etc. There's no industry standard to point to, no broad concept here. Other games do the same thing, but nobody called them signature characters except as reference to WW's' approach to it. D&amp;D has never tagged specific characters as &quot;signature characters&quot; to claim some are and some aren't.<br /> <br /> Outside of WW specific games... it's not a phrase with any distinct meaning. There's no functional way to have a debate over whether X character is or isn't a signature character in Call of Cthulhu the same way you can argue that the Voerman sisters aren't signature characters for VtM despite being iconic Malkavians thanks to the Bloodlines 1 marketing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. One of the distinct points about the World of Darkness is that all characters are pretty much the same on the level of basic fundamentals, and character distinctions are based on lore, politics, and the like. Signature characters are to showcase these distinctions. Conversely, this kind of showcasing isn\u2019t required in, say, <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i>, because the distinction between a fighter and a magic user is encoded at a system level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T15:42:43-07:00","id":1540019,"title":"","content":"Pathfinder's &quot;Iconics&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pathfinderwiki.com/wiki/Iconic\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pathfinderwiki.com/w/images/thumb/2/2a/Iconics_vs_goblins.jpg/1200px-Iconics_vs_goblins.jpg.webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pathfinderwiki.com/wiki/Iconic\" target=\"_blank\"> Iconic - PathfinderWiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pathfinderwiki.com/wiki/Iconic\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pathfinderwiki.com/wiki/Iconic </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T18:06:15-07:00","id":1540022,"title":"","content":"I just find it doubly strange to call Raistlin and Driz'zt &quot;signature characters&quot;, as they're actually departures from expected standards for Player Characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T20:01:26-07:00","id":1540031,"title":"","content":"Personal basis could play apart of it. When magic user comes up in a game the first thought I get is Raistlin Majere from Dragonlance or for great fighters it's the dark elf Drizzt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T01:13:18-07:00","id":1540035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1539997#post1539997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to know that Raistlin was a pregen. Driz'zt, though, is an OC for the novel.<br /> <br /> Either way, neither of them is a Signature Character, even if Driz'zt became a whole trope in itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Elminster is the signature character of the Realms and that's because Ed Greenwood used him as the quest giver in his games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1540022#post1540022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just find it doubly strange to call Raistlin and Driz'zt &quot;signature characters&quot;, as they're actually departures from expected standards for Player Characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the irony is that TSR is the one who started acting like D&amp;D wasn't meant to be utterly insane just like White Wolf eventually did. The first cleric was a vampire and characters at Gary's table included werewolves and robots.<br /> <br /> One of the big failures of White Wolf was the sudden fact that players had to be average and NPCs could be Ur-Shulgi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T02:28:46-07:00","id":1540036,"title":"","content":"The signature characters we're introducing in <b>Curseborne</b> were designed to demonstrate understandable, accessible ways into each Lineage in the game, with Izzy being a temperamental, grungy youth and therefore ideal as a Primal, Eve being a high society blood bathing jet setter and therefore being ideal as a Hungry, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T19:55:33-07:00","id":1540165,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the decision for D&amp;D 3e (and by extension Pathfinder 1e) to have &quot;Iconic&quot; characters for each class was inspired by the &quot;Signature Characters&quot; of White Wolf/WoD?<br /> <br /> Lisa Stevens was the founder of Paizo she's also one of the founders of White Wolf, being part of the OG V1 crew alongside Mark Rein-Hagen, the Wieck Brothers, and Andrew Greenburg. She was one of the players of the :Forged In Steel&quot; playtest campaign that laid the foundations of Chicago By Night. <br /> <br /> IIRC, the very &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas/Supers With Fangs&quot; sample character Malcolm mentioned in the V1 and V2 corebooks was her character for that very same playtest chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T20:50:02-07:00","id":1540167,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if they were inspired by there time at other gamin<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />g companies. Hesha Rudhze served as source of ideas for some of my characters in other settings besides James Bond and Sherlock Holmes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T12:24:51-07:00","id":1540179,"title":"","content":"The bigger name a company has (even if not a terribly big company because TTRPGs aren't big money and all that), the more careful they have to be about using creative elements from other games; esp. games people worked on as freelancers. If there's documented permission that's cool, but in general, the fight over the line between &quot;inspired&quot; and &quot;copied&quot; isn't worth it for most gaming companies to be on either side of, so it's better if the authors don't risk it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T15:40:43-07:00","id":1540185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1540165#post1540165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the decision for D&amp;D 3e (and by extension Pathfinder 1e) to have &quot;Iconic&quot; characters for each class was inspired by the &quot;Signature Characters&quot; of White Wolf/WoD?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly, because their role and development was completely different.<br /> <br /> The &quot;signature characters&quot; for D&amp;D 3rd Edition were playtest character. They were meant to be as generic as possible and had no background. Instead they existed in as many versions as the developers needed to try different material and builds.<br /> <br /> We get in the pictures and texts just a fraction of iterations those characters had, yet it's already a lot of conflicting versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T18:24:55-07:00","id":1540190,"title":"","content":"I also would gather that they don't want said characters to be to similar to avoid legal trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T10:47:34-07:00","id":1540790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539842-how-do-signature-characters-designed?p=1540022#post1540022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just find it doubly strange to call Raistlin and Driz'zt &quot;signature characters&quot;, as they're actually departures from expected standards for Player Characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, clearing up some misconceptions here. Weis and Hickman designed DL1, and when they put it to playtest they gave Raistlin to Terry Phillips. How Phillips' played the character was the inspiration for his his portrayal in the novels. So, in the broadest sense Raistlin was a pregen character, but it's more accurate to say he's a &quot;signature character&quot; in the sense posited by the thread.<br /> <br /> It's not dissimilar to how the main characters of <i>The Expanse</i> book and TV series were &quot;signature characters&quot; of the OGL <i>d20 Future</i> setting Daniel Abraham and Ty Franck were originally developing. That's why and how <i>Leviathan Wakes</i> reads as if it were a novelization of a TTRPG campaign, plot twists, frustrating character decisions, and unexpected events out of nowhere included: it literally was one.<br /> <br /> The only three characters either Franck or Abraham have directly spoken about (to my knowledge) are Holden, Miller, and Shed, and the extent of that were to confirm fans' suspicions (and inside jokes) about each. For Holden it was the &quot;Lawful Stupid D&amp;D paladin&quot; energy, for Shed it was his player having to drop out of nowhere, and for Miller it was his murderhobo moment three-quarters into the book.<br /> <br /> But as far as whether or not Raistlin departs from expectation, he...really doesn't. Raistlin doesn't so much depart from expectation, so much as he represents the most extreme version of it.<br /> <br /> Remember, these were the 1st/2nd edition AD&amp;D days. The days when wizards were universally depicted as paranoid recluses who jealously guarded any and all vestige of arcane power on which they could get their grubby mage hands. And for good reason -- spellbooks weren't character-specific under those rules; there were no rules for easily replacing a lost, stolen, or destroyed spellbook, but plenty for protecting and ciphering a spellbook (including some for which the only use was to protect and/or attack a spellbook); spellbooks and scrolls were incredibly rare finds by most treasure charts, and wizards didn't automatically gain new spells per-level; and wizards were the only arcane caster class. Wizards had the slowest experience progression in the game, and were vulnerable and wholly dependent on the party's protection until at least 6th-8th level.<br /> <br /> As such, there wasn't incentive to play as a jealous, paranoid recluse, so much as absolute necessity.<br /> <br /> Forgotten Realms was the first setting to depict wizards as having an open society in which magic was employed and shared (more or less) freely. The Dragonlance setting <i>predated</i> it by about three years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}